    </span><span class="ͼ13">&gt;</span><span>

    </span><span class="ͼ13">&lt;link</span><span>
        </span><span class="ͼ12">rel</span><span class="ͼv">=</span><span class="ͼz">"icon"</span><span>
        </span><span class="ͼ12">type</span><span class="ͼv">=</span><span class="ͼz">"image/png"</span><span>
        </span><span class="ͼ12">href</span><span class="ͼv">=</span><span class="ͼz">"images/cbra-icon.png"</span><span>
    </span><span class="ͼ13">&gt;</span><span>

</span><span class="ͼ13">&lt;/head&gt;</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<p dir="auto" data-start="1322" data-end="1482">Then refresh the site. <strong data-start="1345" data-end="1394">Chrome sometimes caches favicons aggressively</strong>, so if the globe doesn't immediately disappear, do a hard refresh (<code data-start="1462" data-end="1480">Ctrl + Shift + R</code>).</p>
